  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures a full Mountain Goats performance from Friday, October 3, 2003, at Berbati's Pan in Portland, Oregon [1]. The setlist spans seventeen songs, totaling approximately 65 minutes of music [1]. The program opens with \"First Few Desperate Hours\" and \"Linda Blair Was Born Innocent\" before moving into \"It Froze Me\" and \"Southwood Plantation Road\" [1]. A notable highlight is the inclusion of \"Itzcuintli-Totzli Days,\" a track that has only ten archived performances in the collection [1]. The set continues with \"International Small Arms Traffic Blues,\" \"Your Belgian Things,\" and \"Alpha Incipiens\" [1]. Mid-set, the band plays \"Tallahassee,\" \"Onions,\" and \"Oceanographer's Choice\" [1]. The performance features \"Cheshire County,\" a song described in fan wiki materials as a love song about a cow [3]. The setlist also includes \"Tollund Man,\" \"Shadow Song,\" and \"Cubs in Five\" [1]. A significant moment occurs with the performance of \"Third Snow Song,\" which is marked as a bustout because it appears for the first time in 28 archived shows, a gap of 2,000 days, and is one of only four archived performances of that track [1]. The concert concludes with \"The Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton\" [1]. This specific recording is the only available audio for this date and is the recommended choice for listeners [1]. It is the 49th show in the archive's collection for the band, following a previous archived performance on September 27, 2003, at Mercury [2].",
